--TEST--
an `extend` block may carry `#[Core\Deprecated]` and no other attribute: the second block's `#[Core\Test]` is `E0338`, and the help names `#[Core\Deprecated]` — `rule:classes/an-extend-block-adds-members-to-a-type`
--FILE--
<?nvs
namespace App;

use Core\Time\Date;

#[Core\Deprecated(since: '2.0')]
extend Date as OldDays {
    public function isMonday(): bool {
        return $this->day() == 1;
    }
}

#[Core\Test]
extend Date as BlogDays {
    public function isSunday(): bool {
        return $this->day() == 7;
    }
}

echo "unreachable\n";
// covers: lang:classes/extend-blocks
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0338]: an `extend` block cannot carry this attribute
   --> %s:13:3
   |
13 | #[Core\Test]
   |   ^^^^^^^^^ not allowed on an `extend` block
   = help: delete the attribute. `#[Core\Deprecated]` is the one attribute an `extend` block may carry

error: aborting due to 1 error
%A
